            <ArticleTitle>A novel monoterpenoid indole alkaloid with anticancer activity from Melodinus khasianus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>893-896</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(17)30005-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2017.01.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel monoterpenoid indole alkaloid with unprecedented 6/5/6/4/6 fused rings, khasuanine A (1), was isolated from the roots of Melodinus khasianus. The structure was determined by extensive analysis of its HR-MS, 1D-, and 2D-NMR spectra. Khasuanine A markedly inhibited the proliferation of PC3 cell with IC50 value of 0.45μM. Further study showed that khasuanine A was able to induce the apoptosis of PC3 cells by activation of caspase 3 and p53, and by inhibition of Bcl-2.</AbstractText>
